.TH "ref" 3 "Version 0.9.0" "mbedded-cbor" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
ref \- results that hold the bytes they point into
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SS "Classes"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBcbor::ref< T >\fP"
.br
.RI "A value and a \fRstd::shared_ptr\fP to the owner of the bytes that it views\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBcbor::owning< T >\fP"
.br
.RI "A value that holds its own copy of the bytes of each view in it\&. "
.in -1c
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 
\fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP holds a value and the owner of the bytes that its views point into\&. \fR\fBcbor::owning\fP<T>\fP holds a copy of a value and of the bytes of its views\&. Include \fR<\fBcbor/cbor\&.hpp\fP>\fP\&.

.PP
A text or a byte string comes back as a view into the bytes, and no byte is copied\&. The view sits in a \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP\&. The \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP holds the owner, so the view stays valid while the \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP lives\&.

.PP
A copy of a \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP shares the owner and copies no bytes\&.
.SH "THE OWNER OF THE BYTES"
.PP
The owner is a \fRstd::shared_ptr<void const>\fP\&. Bytes come into the library in one of these forms\&. No form copies the bytes\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
An rvalue \fRstd::string\fP is moved into a new owner\&. \fR\fBcbor::lazy::adopt\fP\fP makes it\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
A \fRstd::shared_ptr<std::string const>\fP is read in place\&. \fR\fBcbor::lazy::view\fP\fP takes it from the caller, and every result keeps it alive\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
A \fRstd::shared_ptr<void const>\fP and a \fRstd::string_view\fP beside it are read in place\&. The owner keeps the bytes of the view alive\&. The library does not check that the owner holds them\&.
.PP

.PP
A \fRstd::string\fP lvalue beside an owner does not compile\&. Its bytes can end before the owner ends\&.

.PP
\fR\fBcbor::structs\fP<T>::decode\fP, \fRcbor::schema<T>::decode\fP, \fRcbor::schema<T>::path\fP and \fR\fBcbor::at_path\fP\fP take the same forms for a view result\&. \fR\fBcbor::sequence\fP\fP takes the two forms that use a \fRstd::shared_ptr\fP, and no rvalue \fRstd::string\fP\&. The library takes no other pointer to bytes\&.

.PP
A larger object can hold the bytes\&. Two forms read them in place\&. The aliasing constructor of \fRstd::shared_ptr\fP makes an owner from a member of the object, and that owner shares the count of the object\&. Or the object is the owner, and a view of its bytes is passed beside it\&.

.PP
A \fR\fBcbor::lazy\fP\fP holds the owner of its bytes\&. So does each \fR\fBcbor::lazy\fP\fP that a step gives, and each iterator of its views\&. A \fR\fBcbor::lazy\fP\fP from a step stays valid after the \fR\fBcbor::lazy\fP\fP that gave it ends\&.
.SH "READ THE VALUE"
.PP
\fR*r\fP gives the value of a \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP \fRr\fP\&. A view comes back by value\&. Any other \fRT\fP comes back as a \fRT const &\fP\&. \fRr->\fP reaches the members of the value\&.

.PP
For a \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<std::string_view>\fP, \fR*r\fP is the \fRstd::string_view\fP\&. The view stays valid while \fRr\fP lives\&. A view copied out of \fRr\fP does not keep the bytes\&. Keep the \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP in a variable as long as its views are in use\&.

.PP
\fR*\fP and \fR->\fP on a temporary \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP do not compile\&. \fR==\fP works on a temporary, because it gives a \fRbool\fP\&. \fR==\fP compares the value with a \fRT\fP, and it compares two \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP by their values\&.
.SH "COPY THE VALUE"
.PP
\fRclone()\fP copies the bytes into new memory\&. The copy stays valid after the owner ends\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
For a \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<std::string_view>\fP, \fRclone()\fP gives a \fRstd::string\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
For a \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<std::span<std::byte const>>\fP, \fRclone()\fP gives a \fRstd::vector<std::byte>\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
For any other \fRT\fP, \fRclone()\fP gives a \fR\fBcbor::owning\fP<T>\fP\&.
.PP
.SH "SHARE AND MOVE"
.PP
A copy of a \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP shares the owner and copies the value\&. A move takes the owner and the value\&. The moved-from \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP holds \fRT{}\fP and no owner\&.

.PP
Only the library makes a \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP\&. A program gets one from a call\&.
.SH "THE OWNING VALUE"
.PP
\fRclone()\fP of a \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP gives a \fR\fBcbor::owning\fP<T>\fP for a \fRT\fP that is not a single text or byte view\&. The \fR\fBcbor::owning\fP<T>\fP holds a copy of the value and of the bytes of each view in it\&. A view in it stays valid while the \fR\fBcbor::owning\fP<T>\fP or one of its copies lives\&.

.PP
\fR*o\fP gives the value as a \fRT const &\fP, and \fRo->\fP reaches its members\&. The value is \fRconst\fP\&. \fR*\fP and \fR->\fP on a temporary \fR\fBcbor::owning\fP<T>\fP do not compile\&.

.PP
A copy of a \fR\fBcbor::owning\fP<T>\fP shares the value and copies no bytes\&. A \fR\fBcbor::owning\fP<T>\fP has no \fR==\fP, and no public constructor\&.
.SH "ERRORS"
.PP
A \fR\fBcbor::ref\fP<T>\fP and a \fR\fBcbor::owning\fP<T>\fP give no error code\&. A wrong use does not compile: \fR*\fP and \fR->\fP on a temporary, and a \fRstd::string\fP lvalue beside an owner\&. A null owner, or an empty owner in the form with a view, given to \fR\fBcbor::lazy::view\fP\fP throws \fRstd::logic_error\fP\&.

.PP
 
.SH "EXAMPLES"
 
.PP
.nf
    // bytes: a std::string with {"name": "ann"}
    {
        auto const doc = cbor::lazy::adopt(std::move(bytes));
        auto const name = doc\->at("name")\->get<std::string_view>();
        if (name)
            kept = *name;  // a copy of the ref: it shares the owner of the bytes
    }  // doc and name end here; kept keeps the bytes
    std::string const copy = kept\->clone();  // "ann", in new memory
.fi
.PP
 
